  "enhanced_information": "The patient is a 23-year-old woman presenting with pleuritic chest pain and tachycardia, with a recent history of air travel, which raises suspicion for pulmonary embolism (PE). The symptoms of pleuritic pain that worsens with deep breaths and tachycardia are consistent with PE. The CT angiogram is the gold standard for diagnosing PE, providing direct visualization of the pulmonary vasculature. While a D-dimer test can help rule out PE, it is less definitive and can yield false positives in other conditions. A chest radiograph is not as effective in diagnosing PE and may not show any abnormalities. Therefore, the most appropriate next test for this patient is a CT angiogram, as it aligns with the consensus for suspected PE in this clinical scenario.",
